  "question": {
    "text": "The number of white coloured salts among the following is .......</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo> </mo><msub><mi>SrSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>Mg</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced><mo> </mo><msub><mi>BaCrO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>Mn</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mfenced><mo> </mo><msub><mi>PbSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mfenced><mo> </mo><msub><mi>PbCrO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>AgBr</mi><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mfenced><mo> </mo><msub><mi>PbI</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mfenced><mo> </mo><msub><mi>CaC</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></mfenced><mo> </mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COO</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The colour of the salts are as follows,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SrSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>- white<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mg</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> - white<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaCrO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> - yellow<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></math> - white<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PbSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> - white<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PbCrO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> - yellow<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgBr</mi></math> - pale yellow<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PbI</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> - yellow<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaC</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> - white</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COO</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> – Brown Red</p><p>Hence the number of salts which are white in colour is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
